"Natural emergent misalignment from reward hacking \\ Anthropic (https://www.anthropic.com/research/emergent-misalignment-reward-hacking)\nciteturn2549view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.anthropic.com/research/emergent-misalignment-reward-hacking\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 86\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn2549view1 [wordlim: 200] Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn2547view0\",\"id\":42}); Total lines: 1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nChatGPT — Release Notes | OpenAI Help Center (https://help.openai.com/en/articles/6825453-chatgpt-release-notes)\nciteturn2549view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn2547view1\",\"pattern\":\"November 21, 2025\"}); Total lines: 2685\nL1385: Update for free and Go users: We’re removing automatic model switching for reasoning in ChatGPT. Previously, some questions were automatically routed to the Thinking model when ChatGPT determined it might help. To maximize choice, free users will now use GPT-5.2 Instant by default, and can still choose to use reasoning anytime by selecting Thinking from the tools menu in the message composer.\nL1386: # November 25, 2025\nL1387: ## An improved Voice interface: the audio you know, with text and visuals when you need them.\nL1388: We’re making ChatGPT Voice a seamless part of the ChatGPT experience, so you can use voice right inside the chat interface you already use every day—no separate mode required.\nL1389: Many of you have asked for a more flexible Voice experience—now, you can speak, listen, and see your conversation at the same time. Answers will be spoken alongside streamed text, image search results, widgets (maps, weather, etc.) and more—right in the same chat thread.\nL1390: This makes voice chats clearer, richer and more contextual by pairing spoken answers with visual context. You can:\nL1391:   * Follow along with typed answers as you listen\nL1392: \nL1393:   * See visual search results like images, charts, and map cards in real time\nL1394: \nL1395:   * Refer back to earlier messages without interrupting the conversation\nL1396: \nL1397:   * Type back when you can’t talk and still get a Voice response\nL1398: \nL1399:   * Share photos to discuss them out loud\nL1400: This means Voice can better adapt to your day and meet you where you are, whether you're practicing a language and seeing words spelled out, need to refer to a measurement while cooking hands-free, or talking through a chart or code sample where visuals help.\nL1401: This update is rolling out to all users globally on the ChatGPT mobile app and chatgpt.com. If you prefer the original Voice experience, you can switch back anytime by going to Settings and turning on “Separate mode” under Voice Mode. We’ll continue listening and refining this experience as we build toward Voice interactions that are both integrated and immersive.\nL1402: # November 24, 2025\nL1403: ## Shopping research in ChatGPT\nL1404: Shopping research is a new interactive experience that helps you find the right products without doing all the research yourself.\nL1405: Describe what you need—like a quiet cordless vacuum for a small apartment, a gift for a four‑year‑old who loves art, or a way to choose between three bikes—and ChatGPT will ask clarifying questions, research deeply across the internet, review quality sources, and build on ChatGPT’s understanding of you from past conversations and memory to return a personalized buyer’s guide with options, tradeoffs, and links to buy.\nL1406: ChatGPT learns what you like through an interactive interface allowing you to guide the research based on your real-time feedback.\nL1407: Shopping research is available on ChatGPT Web, iOS, and Android for logged‑in Free, Go, Plus, and Pro users. To help with holiday shopping, we’re making usage nearly unlimited across plans through the season. To learn more, visit the cite114†blog†openai.com .\nL1408: # November 21, 2025\nL1409: \nL1410: ## More images in answers\nL1411: \nL1412: ChatGPT now adds more inline images from the web to help you quickly understand topics like well-known people, places, and products. When visuals can add clarity, you’ll see images placed beside the relevant paragraph. You can click on any of the images to see them in original dimensions and with the source attribution.\nL1413: These improvements are gradually rolling out globally across all ChatGPT plans, on web, iOS, and Android for responses using GPT 5.1.\nL1414: # November 20, 2025\nL1415: \nL1416: ## Instant Checkout now rolling out to Shopify merchants\nL1417: \nL1418: You can now find and buy from Shopify merchants starting with Spanx, Skims, and Glossier through Instant Checkout in ChatGPT.\nL1419: When a product from a Shopify merchant supports Instant Checkout, you can complete the purchase right in the chat with a quick confirmation of your shipping and payment details.\nL1420: Instant Checkout is available for logged in Plus, Pro, and Free users in the US.\nL1421: \nL1422: # November 19, 2025\nL1423: ## GPT-5.1 Pro: Clearer, more capable answers for complex work\nL1424: Today we’re updating GPT-5 Pro to GPT-5.1 Pro. In early testing, users consistently preferred GPT-5.1 Pro over GPT-5 Pro, rating it especially highly for writing help, data science, and business questions. Testers highlighted the model’s improved clarity, relevance, and structure in its responses.\nL1425: GPT-5.1 Pro is rolling out today for all ChatGPT Pro users and is available in the model picker. GPT-5 Pro will remain available as a legacy model for 90 days before being retired.\nL1426: # November 13, 2025\nL1427: ## Group chats in ChatGPT\nL1428: We’re piloting group chats so you can bring people - and ChatGPT - into the same conversation. Plan trips, make decisions, and collaborate on projects together while ChatGPT helps search, summarize, generate content, and keep everyone on the same page.\nL1429: Group chats are starting to roll out on ChatGPT Web, iOS, and Android in New Zealand, Japan, South Korea, and Taiwan. We’ll use early feedback from this pilot to improve the experience and inform how we expand to more regions and plans over time. To learn more visit the cite115†blog†openai.com .\nL1430: # November 12, 2025\nL1431: ## GPT-5.1 in ChatGPT\nL1432: We’re updating GPT-5 to GPT-5.1 Instant and GPT-5.1 Thinking, making answers both smarter and more conversational. GPT-5.1 Instant now uses light adaptive reasoning for tougher questions while staying fast, and GPT-5.1 Thinking adapts its thinking time more precisely for complex tasks with clearer, less jargony responses.\nL1433: GPT-5.1 Auto continues to route each query to the best model, and GPT-5 models remain available for three months under the Legacy models dropdown so you can compare and transition at your own pace.\nL1434: GPT-5.1 Instant and Thinking are rolling out first to paid (Pro, Plus, Go, Business) users, then to free and logged-out users, with Enterprise and Edu getting a temporary early-access toggle; GPT-5.1 will also be available soon in the API as gpt-5.1-chat-latest (Instant) and gpt-5.1 (Thinking).\nL1435: ## New tone and personalization controls\nL1436: We’re updating ChatGPT’s tone controls so it’s easier to make responses sound the way you prefer. You can now choose from updated presets like Default, Friendly, Efficient, Professional, Candid, and Quirky (with Cynical and Nerdy still available), and we’re experimenting with more granular controls over how concise, warm, or scannable responses are, plus how often emojis appear.\nL1437: Changes you make in Personalization now apply across all chats immediately (including existing conversations), and GPT-5.1 models follow your custom instructions and style preferences more reliably.\nL1438: # November 7, 2025\nL1439: \nL1440: ## Personality and custom instructions now apply to all chats\nL1441: \nL1442: Previously, changes you made to your ChatGPT personality or custom instructions only applied to new conversations. Starting today, updates you make in Settings → Personalization are applied immediately across all chats (including existing conversations!) so your experience stays consistent everywhere without needing to start a new thread.\nL1443: \nL1444: # November 5, 2025\nL1445: ## Interrupt ChatGPT\nL1446: \nL1447: You can now interrupt long-running queries (such as deep research or GPT-5 Pro) to refine what you’re asking—no restart required or progress lost. For example, if you're researching the perfect bookshelf and suddenly remember that your wall is 72\" wide and you can't drill into it, you can simply add that information midstream by clicking “update” in the sidebar and sending the new information as a message. The model will adjust its approach based on your new requirements.\nL1448: # November 3, 2025\nL1449: ## ChatGPT Go Promo - India\nL1450: Eligible customers in India can now get 12 months of ChatGPT Go at no cost. New users can cite116†redeem now on ChatGPT web or the Android app (Google Play). The Apple App Store option arrives next week - no promo code is required for redemption.\nL1451: Available to users in India who are new, on the free plan, or are current ChatGPT Go subscribers - one redemption per account. Requires a payment method (credit card or UPI).\nL1452: If you have an existing ChatGPT Go membership, we may be able to automatically add the promotion for you at the end of your current billing cycle - review cite116†ChatGPT Go Promotion (India) for more details.\nL1453: Update: as of January 21, 2026, the promo has ended\nL1454: # October 30, 2025\nL1455: ## ChatGPT Go expansion\nL1456: \nL1457: We're excited to announce that ChatGPT Go, our low cost subscription plan, is now available in 8 additional countries in Europe, bringing total coverage to cite117†98 countries . The new countries we added are Austria, Czech Republic, Denmark, Norway, Poland, Portugal, Spain and Sweden.\nL1458: For an affordable price, ChatGPT Go provides everything included in the cite73†Free plan, and:\nL1459: \nL1460:   * More messages, larger file uploads, and expanded image generation\nL1461:   * Access to advanced data analysis\nL1462: \nL1463:   * Longer memory for more personalized responses\nL1464: \nL1465: Available on web, mobile (iOS & Android), and desktop (macOS & Windows).\nL1466: Learn more about cite74†ChatGPT Go .\nL1467: ## Credits for Flexible Usage for Codex and Sora\nL1468: \nL1469: Today we’re introducing ways to purchase additional usage in products like Codex and Sora. If you hit your included limits, you can seamlessly buy more credits right in the Codex dashboard or buy more video generations in the Sora app to keep going. Learn more in our article: cite118†Using Credits for Flexible Usage in ChatGPT (Free/Go/Plus/Pro) & Sora. L1470: \nL1471: # October 29, 2025\nL1472: ### ChatGPT Pulse on Web\nL1473: \nL1474: ChatGPT Pulse is now available on web and rolling out to Atlas for Pro users.\nL1475: With Pulse, ChatGPT can do asynchronous research on your behalf once a day based on your past chats, memory, and feedback to help you get things done. The research is delivered to you proactively the next day as a series of visual summaries that you can scan at a glance, expand for more detail, save for later, or ask follow up questions.\nL1476: \nL1477: # October 28, 2025\nL1478: ### ChatGPT Go now available in Brazil\nL1479: \nL1480: We're launching ChatGPT Go, our low cost subscription plan, in Brazil. ChatGPT Go provides everything included in the cite73†Free plan, and:\nL1481: \nL1482:   * More messages, larger file uploads, and expanded image generation\nL1483: \nL1484:   * Access to advanced data analysis\nL1485: \nL1486:   * Longer memory for more personalized responses\nL1487: \nL1488: Available on web, mobile (iOS & Android), and desktop (macOS & Windows).\nL1489: Learn more about cite74†ChatGPT Go .\nL1490: \nL1491: # October 23, 2025\nL2106: ## Web and the Windows desktop app\nL2107: \nL2108: 1⁠. In-line message error retries: If you encounter a message error, you can retry or just continue chatting in the same conversation.\nL2109: \nL2110: cite171†Image: ChatGPT conversation with a failed response and Retry button†images.ctfassets.net L2111: 2⁠. o1 and o3-mini now offer Python-powered data analysis in ChatGPT: You can now ask these models to perform tasks like running regressions on test data, visualizing complex business metrics, and conducting scenario-based simulations.\nL2112: 3⁠. Conversation Drafts: Unsubmitted messages in your message prompt will now be saved.\nL2113: \nL2114: cite172†Image: ChatGPT Projects conversation list with a draft reply being composed†images.ctfassets.net L2115: 4⁠. New UI for Temporary Chats: We’ve made accessing and viewing these private conversations more clear.\nL2116: \nL2117: cite173†Image: ChatGPT Temporary Chat mode active, noting chats are not saved to history or memory†images.ctfassets.net L2118: ## Android App\nL2119: \nL2120: 1⁠. Increased the default size for in‐line generated images.\nL2121: \nL2122: cite174†Image: Image†images.ctfassets.net L2123: \nL2124: 2⁠. More clear and private Incognito keyboard for Temporary Chats.\nL2125: \nL2126: cite175†Image: ChatGPT Android app Temporary chat screen with notice that chats are not saved to history or used to train models†images.ctfassets.net L2127: ## iOS App\nL2128: \nL2129: 1⁠. Improved table-copying functionality out of ChatGPT responses on iOS and macOS.\nL2130: \nL2131: cite176†Image: ChatGPT 4o research response with a grocery price table copied into Google Sheets†images.ctfassets.net L2132: \nL2133: 2⁠. Added long press on your message to open menu actions: Copy, Edit.\nL2134: \nL2135: cite177†Image: What’s new? prompt with a context menu offering Copy and Edit†images.ctfassets.net L2136: \nL2137: 3⁠. Improved response display of nested blockquote content.\nL2138: cite178†Image: ChatGPT mobile chat with examples of Markdown blockquotes†images.ctfassets.net L2139: \nL2140: 4⁠. Improved display and faster streaming of conversations and message menu actions.\nL2141: \nL2142: cite179†Image: ChatGPT 4o mobile chat replying to “Hey what’s up”†images.ctfassets.net L2143: # February 28, 2025\nL2144: \nL2145:   * General\nL2146: \nL2147:   * iOS\nL2148: \nL2149:   1. Long press to select text on iOS and moved the message quick actions to always be visible below the message:\nL2150: \nL2151: cite180†Image: ChatGPT iPhone app with selected reply text and the iOS text menu open†images.ctfassets.net L2152: \nL2153: ⁠   2⁠. Bug fixes and small improvements in the cite181†1.2025.056 iOS release†apps.apple.com .\nL2154: ⁠   3⁠. A setting to allow users to auto-submit transcriptions.\nL2155: ⁠     1⁠. OFF by default.\nL2156: \nL2157:   * Android\nL2158:   1. Improved error handling for Play Integrity errors.\nL2159: # February 21, 2025\nL2160: \nL2161: 1⁠. iOS widget (see below):\nL2162: \nL2163: cite182†Image: iPhone ChatGPT widget with Message ChatGPT plus camera, photo, voice, and microphone shortcuts†images.ctfassets.net L2164: \nL2165: 2⁠. Text selection improvements: you can now select text across horizontal rulers. 3. Performance improvements: Improved model header loading behavior. Conversation history and GPTs show up faster. 4. Bug fix for logged-out users: 401s when dismissing tooltips. 401s logging out users on Android.\nL2166: # February 14, 2025\nL2167: \nL2168:   * Set ChatGPT as default search engine in Safari.\nL2169: \nL2170:   * Confirmation dialog for logging out (iOS, web).\nL2171: \nL2172:   * Improved Android conversation parsing performance.\nL2173: \nL2174:   * iOS performance fixes.\nL2175: \nL2176:   * Updated launch animations and composer design on Android.\nL2177: \nL2178:   * Whisper (ChatGPT's voice-to-text feature) now shows a text preview of dictated text after recording:\nL2179: \nL2180: cite183†Image: Voice recording bar with transcript preview, waveform, and 0:02 duration†images.ctfassets.net L2181: \nL2182: # February 6, 2025\nL2183: ## Canvas sharing\nL2184: \nL2185: Users can now share a Canvas asset such as rendered React/HTML code, document, or code with another user, similar to how you share a conversation. You can do this from the Canvas toolbar when Canvas is open.\nL2186: \nL2187: cite184†Image: Canvas preview titled Floaty Bubbles With Background with dot text reading SHARING NOW AVAILABLE†images.ctfassets.net L2188: \nL2189: For more details about the canvas feature in ChatGPT, check out the following Help Center article!\nL2190: \nL2191: # January 17, 2025\nL2192: ## More personalization in Custom Instructions\nL2193: We've updated custom instructions to make it easier to customize how ChatGPT responds to you. With the new UI, you can tell ChatGPT the traits you want it to have, how you want it to talk to you, and any rules you want it to follow.\nL2194: If you're already using custom instructions, this won't change your current settings.\nL2195: The new UI is rolling out now on cite112†http://chatgpt.com†chatgpt.com and desktop on Windows, and is coming to mobile and desktop on macOS in the next few weeks. Available soon to ChatGPT users in the EU, Norway, Iceland, Liechtenstein, and Switzerland.\nL2196: cite185†Image: Image†images.ctfassets.net L2197: # January 15, 2025\nL2198: \nL2199: ## Import from Chat into Canvas\nL2200: \nL2201:   * Edit a full model response in Canvas\nL2202: \nL2203:   * Edit a code block in Canvas\nL2204: \nL2205: Web only (no desktop or mobile in this release).\nL2206: \nL2207: # January 14, 2025\nL2208: ## Scheduled tasks in ChatGPT\nL2209: \nL2210: Today we’re rolling out a beta version of tasks—a new way to ask ChatGPT to do things for you at a future time. Whether it's one-time reminders or recurring actions, tell ChatGPT what you need and when, and it will automatically take care of it.\nL2211: Scheduled tasks is in early beta for Plus, Pro, and Teams. Eventually this will be available to anyone with a ChatGPT account.\nL2212: For details see Scheduled tasks in ChatGPT.\nL2213: \nL2214: # December 13, 2024\nL2215: ## Projects in ChatGPT\nL2216: \nL2217: Projects provide a new way to group files and chats for personal use, simplifying the management of work that involves multiple chats. You can set custom instructions and upload files in your Projects, and any conversations in your Project share context with your uploaded files and custom instructions. Chats in Projects use GPT-4o and support the following features:\nL2218: \nL2219:   * Canvas\nL2220: \nL2221:   * Advanced data analysis\nL2222: \nL2223:   * DALL•E\nL2224: \nL2225:   * Search\nL2226: ChatGPT Projects are available to all Plus, Team, and Pro users.\nL2227: # Dec 12, 2024\nL2228: ## Santa Voice and Video and Screen Share in Voice Chats\nL2229: \nL2230: Today we started rolling out two updates to voice mode in ChatGPT:\nL2231: \nL2232:   * Santa voice: You can now chat with Santa in ChatGPT! Until early January, you can find Santa in the list of available voices in settings or by tapping on a snowflake icon. We are rolling out Santa globally to all logged in users today, and you can chat with Santa everywhere you use voice mode.\nL2233: The first time you chat with Santa, your advanced voice limit will reset one time. So, if you’ve already used up your advanced voice limit for the day or the month (based on your subscription plan), you can still chat with Santa for the first time using advanced voice.\nL2234: \nL2235: cite186†Image: Santa theme card with snowy blue artwork and the subtitle Merry and bright†images.ctfassets.net L2236:   * Video and screenshare: In our latest mobile apps, we are starting to roll out real-time video, screen share, and image upload capabilities in advanced voice. We expect to complete this rollout to all Team and most Plus and Pro users, except for those in the European Union, Switzerland, Iceland, Norway, and Liechtenstein, over the next week. Video and screen share are subject to daily usage limits for all plans, and image uploads are subject to ChatGPT vision message limits.\nL2237: Use the controls at the bottom of the screen, like the camera button below, to get started. You can find screen share and image upload controls under the “...” menu at the bottom of the screen.\nL2238: \nL2239: cite187†Image: Image†images.ctfassets.net L2240: # Dec 10, 2024\nL2241: ## Canvas\nL2242: \nL2243: Today we made Canvas available in 4o by default for all users, Free and Paid. Additionally, we launched a number of new capabilities for canvas, including:\nL2244: \nL2245:   * Canvas in GPTs: Canvas can now be used with GPTs when enabled in the GPT creator. This toggle will be enabled for newly created GPTs by default.\nL2246: \nL2247: cite188†Image: Capabilities list with Canvas selected and Web Search, DALL·E Image Generation, and Code Interpreter unchecked†images.ctfassets.net L2248:   * Python code execution: You can now execute Python code in a canvas. ChatGPT will take a pass on fixing bugs in your code and provide comments on errors.\nL2249: \nL2250:   * Canvas shortcut: You can now paste content into ChatGPT and instantly open it in canvas via a shortcut in the upper right corner of the composer.\nL2251: \nL2252:     * ⁠\nL2253: \nL2254:   * Canvas in Toolbox: Canvas has been added as an option in the toolbox.\nL2255: \nL2256: cite189†Image: ChatGPT composer with the tools menu open, highlighting Picture for DALL·E†images.ctfassets.net L2332: # May 13, 2024\nL2333: \nL2334: ## Introducing GPT-4o\nL2335: \nL2336: GPT-4o is our newest flagship model that provides GPT-4-level intelligence that is much faster and improves on its capabilities across text, voice, and vision. Currently, only the new text and image capabilities have been rolled out. You can read more about the announcement here.\nL2337: Plus users will have a message limit that is up to 5x greater than free users, and Team and Enterprise users will have even higher limits.\nL2338: \nL2339: # Apr 29, 2024\nL2340: ## Memory is now available to Plus users\nL2341: \nL2342: Memory is now available to all ChatGPT Plus users, except in Europe Korea where we will be rolling it out soon. Using Memory is easy: just start a new chat and tell ChatGPT anything you’d like it to remember.\nL2343: Memory can be turned on or off in settings. Team, Enterprise, and GPTs to come.\nL2344: \nL2345: # Apr 1, 2024\nL2346: ## Start using ChatGPT instantly\nL2347: \nL2348: We’re making it easier for people to experience the benefits of AI without needing to sign up. Starting today, you can use ChatGPT instantly, without needing to sign-up. We're rolling this out gradually, with the aim to make AI accessible to anyone curious about its capabilities.\nL2349: \nL2350: # Feb 13, 2024\nL2351: ## Memory and new controls for ChatGPT\nL2352: We’re testing memory with ChatGPT. Remembering things you discuss across all chats saves you from having to repeat information and makes future conversations more helpful.\nL2353: You're in control of ChatGPT's memory. You can explicitly tell it to remember something, ask it what it remembers, and tell it to forget conversationally or through settings. You can also turn it off entirely.\nL2354: We are rolling out to a small portion of ChatGPT free and Plus users this week to learn how useful it is. We will share plans for a broader roll out soon.\nL2355: You can read more about memory and controls here.\nL2356: # Jan 10, 2024\nL2357: \nL2358: ## Introducing the GPT Store and ChatGPT Team plan\nL2359: \nL2360: #### Discover what’s trending in the GPT Store\nL2361: \nL2362: The store features a diverse range of GPTs developed by our partners and the community. Browse popular and trending GPTs on the community leaderboard, with categories like DALL·E, writing, research, programming, education, and lifestyle.\nL2363: Explore GPTs at chatgpt.com/gpts.\nL2364: #### Use ChatGPT alongside your team\nL2365: We’re launching a new ChatGPT plan for teams of all sizes, which provides a secure, collaborative workspace to get the most out of ChatGPT at work.\nL2366: ChatGPT Team offers access to our advanced models like GPT-4 and DALL·E 3, and tools like Advanced Data Analysis. It additionally includes a dedicated collaborative workspace for your team and admin tools for team management. As with ChatGPT Enterprise, you own and control your business data — we do not train on your business data or conversations, and our models don’t learn from your usage. More details on our data privacy practices can be found on our privacy page and Trust Portal.\nL2367: You can learn more about the ChatGPT Team plan here.\nL2368: # November 21, 2023\nL2369: \nL2370: ## ChatGPT with voice is available to all users\nL2371: \nL2372: ChatGPT with voice is now available to all free users. Download the app on your phone and tap the headphones icon to start a conversation.\nL2373: \nL2374: # November 6, 2023\nL2375: ## Introducing GPTs\nL2376: You can now create custom versions of ChatGPT that combine instructions, extra knowledge, and any combination of skills. Learn more here.\nL2377: We’re rolling out custom versions of ChatGPT that you can create for a specific purpose—called GPTs. GPTs are a new way for anyone to create a tailored version of ChatGPT to be more helpful in their daily life, at specific tasks, at work, or at home—and then share that creation with others. For example, GPTs can help you learn the rules to any board game, help teach your kids math, or design stickers.\nL2378: Plus and Enterprise users can start creating GPTs this week. Later this month, we’ll launch the GPT Store, so people can feature and make money from their GPTs. We plan to offer GPTs to more users soon.\nL2379: # October 17, 2023\nL2380: \nL2381: ## Browsing is now out of beta\nL2382: \nL2383: Browsing, which we re-launched a few weeks ago, is moving out of beta.\nL2384: Plus and Enterprise users no longer need to switch the beta toggle to use browse, and are able to choose \"Browse with Bing\" from the GPT-4 model selector.\nL2385: \nL2386: # October 16, 2023\nL2387: ## DALL·E 3 is now rolling out in beta\nL2388: \nL2389: We’ve integrated DALL·E 3 with ChatGPT, allowing it to respond to your requests with images. From a simple sentence to a detailed paragraph, ask ChatGPT what you want to see and it will translate your ideas into exceptionally accurate images.\nL2390: To use DALL·E 3 on both web and mobile, choose DALL·E 3 in the selector under GPT-4. The message limit may vary based on capacity.\nL2391: \nL2392: # September 27, 2023\nL2393: ## Browsing is rolling back out to Plus users\nL2394: \nL2395: Browsing is rolling out to all Plus users. ChatGPT can now browse the internet to provide you with current and authoritative information, complete with direct links to sources. It is no longer limited to data before September 2021.\nL2396: To try it out, enable Browsing in your beta features setting.\nL2397: \nL2398:   * Click on 'Profile & Settings’\nL2399: \nL2400:   * Select 'Beta features'\nL2401: \nL2402:   * Toggle on ‘Browse with Bing’\nL2403: \nL2404: Choose Browse with Bing in the selector under GPT-4.\nL2405: # September 25, 2023\nL2406: \nL2407: ## New voice and image capabilities in ChatGPT\nL2408: \nL2409: We are beginning to roll out new voice and image capabilities in ChatGPT. They offer a new, more intuitive type of interface by allowing you to have a voice conversation or show ChatGPT what you’re talking about. Learn more here.\nL2410: #### Voice (Beta) is now rolling out to Plus users on iOS and Android\nL2411: \nL2412: You can now use voice to engage in a back-and-forth conversation with your assistant. Speak with it on the go, request a bedtime story, or settle a dinner table debate.\nL2413: To get started with voice, head to Settings → New Features on the mobile app and opt into voice conversations. Then, tap the headphone button located in the top-right corner of the home screen and choose your preferred voice out of five different voices.\nL2414: #### Image input will be generally available to Plus users on all platforms\nL2415: \nL2416: You can now show ChatGPT one or more images. Troubleshoot why your grill won’t start, explore the contents of your fridge to plan a meal, or analyze a complex graph for work-related data. To focus on a specific part of the image, you can use the drawing tool in our mobile app.\nL2417: To get started, tap the photo button to capture or choose an image. You can also discuss multiple images or use our drawing tool to guide your assistant.\nL2418: # September 11, 2023\nL2419: ## ChatGPT language support - Alpha on web\nL2420: \nL2421: ChatGPT now supports a limited selection of languages in the interface:\nL2422: \nL2423:   * Chinese (zh-Hans)\nL2424: \nL2425:   * Chinese (zh-TW)\nL2426: \nL2427:   * French (fr-FR)\nL2428: \nL2429:   * German (de-DE)\nL2430: \nL2431:   * Italian (it-IT)\nL2432: \nL2433:   * Japanese (ja-JP)\nL2434: \nL2435:   * Portuguese (pt-BR)\nL2436: \nL2437:   * Russian (ru-RU)\nL2438: \nL2439:   * Spanish (es-ES)\nL2440: If you've configured your browser to use one of these supported languages, you'll see a banner in ChatGPT that enables you to switch your language settings. You can deactivate this option at any time through the settings menu.\nL2441: This feature is in alpha, requires opting in, and currently can only be used on the web at chatgpt.com. Learn more here.\nL2442: # August 28, 2023\nL2443: \nL2444: ## Introducing ChatGPT Enterprise\nL2445: \nL2446: Today we’re launching ChatGPT Enterprise, which offers enterprise-grade security and privacy, unlimited higher-speed GPT-4 access, longer context windows for processing longer inputs, advanced data analysis capabilities, customization options, and much more.\nL2447: ChatGPT Enterprise also provides unlimited access to Advanced Data Analysis, previously known as Code Interpreter.\nL2448: Learn more on our website and connect with our sales team to get started.\nL2449: # August 21, 2023\nL2450: \nL2451: ## Custom instructions are now available to users in the EU & UK\nL2452: \nL2453: Custom instructions are now available to users in the European Union United Kingdom.\nL2454: To add your instructions:\nL2455: \nL2456:   * Click on your name\nL2457: \nL2458:   * Select ‘Custom instructions’\nL2459: \nL2460: # August 9, 2023\nL2461: ## Custom instructions are now available to free users\nL2462: \nL2463: Custom instructions are now available to ChatGPT users on the free plan, except for in the EU UK where we will be rolling it out soon!\nL2464: Customize your interactions with ChatGPT by providing specific details and guidelines for your chats.\nL2465: To add your instructions:\nL2466: \nL2467:   * Click on your name\nL2468: \nL2469:   * Select ‘Custom instructions’\nL2470: \nL2471: # August 3, 2023\nL2472: ## Updates to ChatGPT\nL2473: We’re rolling out a bunch of small updates to improve the ChatGPT experience. Shipping over the next week:\nL2474: 1⁠. Prompt examples: A blank page can be intimidating. At the beginning of a new chat, you’ll now see examples to help you get started.\nL2475: 2⁠. Suggested replies: Go deeper with a click. ChatGPT now suggests relevant ways to continue your conversation.\n"
